    <tags>parquet csv json data viewer tui terminal sql duckdb</tags>
    <summary>A fast, read-only viewer for Parquet, CSV, TSV and JSON data files.</summary>
    <description>
Peruse opens a data file in the terminal and shows it as a table. It reads
Parquet, CSV, TSV and JSON, and it reads a file that is larger than the memory
of the machine.

You can sort a column, filter the rows with a builder or with SQL, search the
text, read one record on its own, open the structures inside a JSON value, and
see the metadata and the statistics of each column. It can also write the DDL
for a table in Oracle, MySQL, Snowflake, PostgreSQL and others from the shape
of the file.

Peruse never writes to your file. It opens it read-only, and it refuses any
statement that would change data.

### Licences

The program holds DuckDB and 26 C and C++ libraries. THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md,
which is installed beside the program, names each one. Every licence is
permissive.
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/JohnGrey0/peruse/releases/tag/v__VERSION__</releaseNotes>
